[3:21:47 PM] [semantic-release] [@semantic-release/commit-analyzer] › ℹ  Analyzing commit: ci(APP-785): add shadow-mode PR-gated release flow for app-backend

Adds a PR-gated release/hotfix/rollback flow modelled on the frontend, adapted to
the backend

New workflows:
- deploy-reusable: workflow_call build-on-server deploy; environment: is the approval gate
- release-start: dry-run version -> release/x.y.z -> bump + CHANGELOG -> PR -> Slack root
- release-pr: fast checks + staging deploy (Approve #1) + non-blocking E2E
- release-finalize: tag + GitHub Release from CHANGELOG, carries the Slack thread
- app-production: prod deploy (CI Gate) + E2E + idempotent main->development back-merge
- release-cancel, hotfix-start (manual), rollback, develop-deploy
- CODEOWNERS for Approve #2

Landed in SHADOW MODE: targets a throwaway test-release branch + sandbox env, so the
live release.yml (semantic-release on push:main) is untouched. Flip steps and the
dry-run guide are in .github/workflows/RELEASE_FLOW_SHADOW.md.
