Route DexQuoterModule RPC calls (readErc20Decimals, quoteV3, quoteV2) through
a new per-network getDexQuoterLimiter so rate-fetching can't contend with the
indexer for slots on the shared node limiter. Conservative defaults
(maxConcurrent=5, minTime=200ms) since DEX quoting is bulk and low priority.
[3:21:47 PM] [semantic-release] [@semantic-release/commit-analyzer] › ℹ  The release type for the commit is minor
[3:21:47 PM] [semantic-release] [@semantic-release/commit-analyzer] › ℹ  Analyzing commit: feat(rates): use DEX quoter to price tokens on non-CoinGecko chains (BE-205)

CoinGecko's per-token endpoint requires the network to be in its networksMap;
for chains like Citrea every ERC-20 lookup returned false and priceUsd stayed
at 0. Wire DexQuoterModule into FetchRates as the pricing source for these
chains and short-circuit the wasted CoinGecko call. Native tokens still use
CoinGecko's /coins/{id} path. shouldSkipFetch is now DEX-aware so tokens on
quoter-enabled networks aren't marked skip just because CoinGecko has nothing.
[3:21:47 PM] [semantic-release] [@semantic-release/commit-analyzer] › ℹ  The release type for the commit is minor
[3:21:47 PM] [semantic-release] [@semantic-release/commit-analyzer] › ℹ  Analyzing commit: fix(dex-quoter): make public APIs return null on infra/config failures (BE-205)

Address Copilot review on PR #1329:

- readErc20Decimals: wrap in try/catch and guard missing provider; return null
  instead of throwing on non-ERC20 tokens or RPC outage. Sanity-check the
  reported decimals before exponentiating.
- quoteV3 / quoteV2: guard against undefined provider before constructing the
  Contract instance, so a network with no configured RPC bails to null instead
  of crashing the entire getQuote path.
- getQuote: when default amountIn cannot be derived (decimals read fails),
  warn and return null rather than throwing 10n ** BigInt(NaN).
- getRateInNative: warn-log DEX entries whose wrappedNative diverges from
  dexes[0] so a config drift can't silently quote against the wrong denominator.

Integration spec: drop describe.skip in favor of runtime skip when
CITREA_TEST_TOKEN_ADDRESS env var is unset, so the suite stays disabled by
default but can be enabled without a code change once a liquid token is wired.

Adds 4 unit tests covering: missing-provider in getQuote/getRateInNative,
decimals-throws in getQuote, mismatched-wrappedNative warning path. All 18
dexQuoter unit tests pass.
