[3:21:47 PM] [semantic-release] [@semantic-release/commit-analyzer] › ℹ  Analyzing commit: feat(logger): hide RPC API keys in URLs sent to logz.io and sentry (#1257)

The external transport now scrubs API keys embedded in URLs from the
log payload before it leaves the process. Three URL formats this
codebase actually uses are handled:

- Alchemy:  alchemy.com/v2/<key>        -> .../v2/[REDACTED]
- dRPC:     ?dkey=<key>                 -> ?dkey=[REDACTED]
- Ankr:     rpc.ankr.com/<chain>/<key>  -> .../[REDACTED]

Redaction runs on a serialized JSON snapshot of the log payload built
inside ExternalLogger.log(), never on the live winston `info` object.
Winston shares that reference across all transports (console + external),
so in-place mutation would bleed into local console output, and some
libraries like ethers define own Error properties (e.g. `code` on a
TypeError from `invalid address`) as read-only which makes even a
no-op assignment throw. The serialized form is a plain object with
neither Error instances nor frozen properties, so `redactPayload`
can walk it safely.

- src/logger/redact.ts: redactUrlKeys() for individual strings,
  redactPayload() walks plain objects/arrays in place. String
  assignment is guarded with `if (redacted !== current)` so no-op
  writes are never attempted.
- src/logger/external.ts: scrub each of the two downstream paths
  (logzio, sentry) independently. For Sentry, construct a fresh
  Error with a redacted message/stack instead of mutating
  info.error. Both paths are wrapped in their own try/catch with
  a try/finally around the winston callback, so any serialization
  or transport failure is swallowed locally — broken logs must
  not tear down the app.
- test/unit/logger/redact.spec.ts: 13 tests covering each URL
  pattern, negative cases, nested structures, Error instances
  flowing through unchanged, a non-writable `code` property
  (mirroring the ethers TypeError shape), circular refs, and
  primitive inputs.
- test/unit/logger/external.spec.ts: the two Sentry assertions
  now check scalar fields on the serialized extras snapshot
  (level, message, errorMessage, userId) instead of deep-equalling
  the live log reference.
