[3:21:47 PM] [semantic-release] [@semantic-release/commit-analyzer] › ℹ  Analyzing commit: fix(assets): route Citrea token balances through Blockscout v2 (#1261)

* fix(assets): route Citrea token balances through Blockscout v2

Alchemy's Enhanced API (`alchemy_getTokenBalances`) is disabled on Citrea
and returns `-32600 "EAPIs not enabled on specified network:
[CITREA_MAINNET]"`. `Web3Helper.getTokenBalances` swallows that into an
empty array, which is why every Citrea DAO in the UI shows no ERC20
assets — only the native cBTC balance row is ever written.

Citrea Blockscout also rejects the legacy Etherscan-compat path
`?module=account&action=addresstokenbalance` with HTTP 400, but its
modern REST v2 endpoint `/api/v2/addresses/{addr}/token-balances`
returns strictly-typed ERC-20 balances with full metadata.

Changes:

- `evmExplorerClient.getTokenBalances` branches on BLOCKSCOUT and
  dispatches to a new private `getBlockscoutV2TokenBalances` that hits
  the v2 REST endpoint, filters to ERC-20 only (skipping ERC-721 /
  ERC-1155 entries), and normalizes through the same
  `utils.parseTokenBalance` as the legacy path. Non-Blockscout explorers
  continue to use the Etherscan-compat route untouched.

- `Web3Provider.getTokenBalances` routes `citreaMainnet` to
  `evmExplorerClient.getTokenBalances(BLOCKSCOUT, …)` — same pattern
  the file already uses for `fetchContractCreation` and
  `fetchContractSourceCode`. The explorer path skips
  `handleAlchemyCrazyBalance` because Blockscout v2 returns already-parsed
  decimal strings; all other chains keep the Alchemy path verbatim.

- New unit-dep integration test hits real Citrea Blockscout, asserts the
  JUCY 5e18 deposit is returned with correct metadata, runtime ~430ms.

No code change needed for non-Citrea chains. This only affects networks
explicitly routed through `EvmExplorerEnum.BLOCKSCOUT` — currently just
Citrea — so Ethereum/Polygon/Base/Arbitrum/etc. continue to use
Alchemy's Enhanced API unchanged.

* test(citrea-blockscout): drop .only and weaken exact-balance assertion

- Remove `describe.only` which was tripping `yarn test:dotonly` in CI
  (dot-only-hunter). The `.only` was left in from local debugging.

- Replace the exact-value check on `originalBalance === '5000000000000000000'`
  with a shape + positive-balance assertion. Any JUCY transfer in or out
  of the DAO would have flipped the exact match to a flake; the intent
  was always to prove the Blockscout path returns a usable row, not to
  pin an on-chain balance.

Addresses Copilot review on #1261 (comments #2 and #3). Copilot's third
suggestion — renaming `.env.unit-deep` to `.env.unit-dep` — is ignored
because the env file is literally named `.env.unit-deep` on disk, the
project uses inconsistent naming (`test/unit-dep/` directory + `.env.unit-deep` file).

* test(citrea-blockscout): unit coverage for Blockscout v2 branch

Adds coverage for the two new code paths introduced in 04893cc6 so
nyc thresholds (branches 90%, functions 97.97%) go back to green:

- test/unit/helpers/evmExplorerClient.spec.ts — 8 new tests covering
  getBlockscoutV2TokenBalances: success + normalization, /api suffix
  stripping, ERC-721 filtering via token_id, zero-balance filtering,
  missing address_hash/decimals, non-array response, axios failure
  handling, unsupported-network guard.

- test/unit/modules/proxyProvider/web3Provider.spec.ts — 2 new tests
  covering the citreaMainnet branch: routing to evmExplorerClient with
  BLOCKSCOUT, bypassing Web3Helper.getTokenBalances and
  handleAlchemyCrazyBalance, and the ProxyToken-not-found filter on
  the explorer path.

No production code changes.

* style: apply biome format to the expectedUrl constant
