[3:21:47 PM] [semantic-release] [@semantic-release/commit-analyzer] › ℹ  Analyzing commit: feat(crawler): per-network MAX_BLOCK_RANGE cap + Citrea transfer sync test (#1258)

Citrea mainnet's RPC caps eth_getLogs to a 1000-block window, but the
adaptive batch size manager's day-based math always produced ranges
over that limit (60-day initial, 0.05-day floor still > 1000 blocks at
2s per block). The crawler hit -32602 on every batch and Citrea DAOs
synced zero transfers. The same code path also fails silently on any
DAO whose RPC has no provider configured (Web3Helper.getBlockNumber
returns -1, the crawler scans 5471881 → -1 and "succeeds" with 0 logs).

Changes
- Add MAX_BLOCK_RANGE to every per-network entry in config.NODES.
  Defaults: 10000 for Alchemy/Infura-friendly chains, 5000 for chiliz,
  2048 for avax public RPC, 1000 for citrea. All overridable via
  NODES_<NETWORK>_MAX_BLOCK_RANGE env var.
- Extend IRawNodeConfig with the new field.
- AdaptiveBatchSizeManager reads the per-network cap in its
  constructor and applies it via a new capToMaxBlockRange() helper.
  The cap is enforced in calculateBatchSizeInBlocks, the constructor's
  initial sizing, the sparse-region jump in recordSuccess, and
  getSkipAheadBatchSize, so no code path can produce a range above
  the RPC's hard limit.

Verification
- New unit-dep suite "Integration: DAO Transaction Service - Citrea"
  in test/unit-dep/daoTransaction.spec.ts. It stubs MongoDB.drop so
  the global beforeEach does not wipe the connected DB, upserts the
  citrea-mainnet DAO 0x10FD…6dB2, runs the real DaoTransactions.start
  against Alchemy, and asserts that the JUCY (5.0) ERC20 deposit
  appears in Models.Transaction.
- Test passes against Alchemy with NODES_CITREA_MAINNET_ALCHEMY_API_KEY
  set: scans 5471881 → 6032566 in ~3 minutes with 1000-block batches,
  finds tx 0x62fda5cc…58d at block 5814770.
