[3:21:47 PM] [semantic-release] [@semantic-release/commit-analyzer] › ℹ  Analyzing commit: feat(BE-163): scoped retryAll for crawler RPC errors (#1186)

* feat(BE-163): scoped retryAll for crawler RPC errors

Add retryAll option to retryRequest helper so crawler paths retry all
errors (not just whitelisted ones) before giving up. This prevents
transient RPC errors like HTTP 520 from triggering Slack alerts
immediately and from being misclassified as batch-size errors.

- Add retryAll?: boolean to RetryOptions (default false, zero change for other callers)
- Pass retryAll: true in batchRequestManager (3 call sites) and blockchainLogCrawler (2 call sites)
- Downgrade provider.ts invalid JSON/empty response logs from error to warn
- Remove duplicate logger.error block in blockchainLogCrawler.getLogsWithoutTopics
- Remove transient JSON errors from batch-size error whitelists (config + crawlerErrorHandler)
- Add unit tests for retryAll behavior

* fix(BE-163): update blockchainLogCrawler tests for retryAll behavior

Tests now expect retryRequest to exhaust retries before throwing
(since retryAll: true retries all errors). Updated 7 test assertions
to expect "Request failed after N retries" instead of the original
error, and stub Utils.wait to avoid delays.

* fix(BE-163): register GaugeVoter ABI in DecodeActions

GaugeVoter artifact was not registered in _setupSignatures(), causing
updateGaugeMetadata/registerGauge/createGauge actions to decode as
'Unknown' instead of their proper types.

* fix(test): update allSignatures count to 18 after adding GaugeVoter

* fix(retryRequest): add skipRetry callback to prevent retrying batch size errors

Batch size errors should not be retried — they need to reach the caller
so adaptive batch size reduction can kick in. Without skipRetry, retryAll
wraps the original error in "Request failed after N retries", breaking
isBatchSizeError() matching in executeBatchRequest and getLogsWithoutTopics.

* test: remove isBatchSizeError stubs to test real behavior, strengthen onError assertion

- Remove isBatchSizeError stubs in getLogsWithoutTopics tests since real
  error messages already match batch size patterns via skipRetry
- Add error assertion on onError callback to verify error details are preserved

* fix(retryRequest): preserve original error on exhaustion, remove broad 'retry' pattern

Two critical fixes:

1. retryRequest now re-throws the last original error (with retryCount added)
   instead of a generic "Request failed after N retries". This preserves
   error.code, error.response, error.config etc. so downstream consumers
   (onError callbacks, error classifiers) can inspect the real error.

2. Removed 'retry' from ERROR_BATCH_SIZE config — it was too broad and
   would match the old "Request failed after N retries" message, causing
   every exhausted-retry error to be silently misclassified as a batch
   size error. 'Please retry' (more specific) is still in the list.

* fix(batchRequest): enhance error handling for batch requests and classify errors correctly

* test(batchRequest): remove exclusive test flags for batch request integration tests

* test(batchRequest): enable batch request integration test and remove skipped error handling test

* refactor(batchRequest): remove unused imports from batch request tests

* fix(retryRequest): prioritize skipRetry option over serverNotAvailableError

